lational/descriptive pairing section\n   204→  - Log top relational/descriptive names found\n   205→  - Log top proper names used for pairing\n   206→  - Flag critical pairs like \"my father\" + \"Alphonse Frankenstein\" with INFO level\n   207→\n   208→**Testing:** All 444 tests pass.\n   209→\n   210→**Result:** FAILED - No improvement, same issues as Attempt 3\n   211→- ❌ \"my father\" (54), \"Father\" (6), \"M.\" (23), \"M. Frankenstein\" (2), \"Alphonse Frankenstein\" (1) STILL separate\n   212→- ❌ William Frankenstein STILL missing from character list (present in Ch. 8 summary)\n   213→- ❌ \"Clerval\" (55) and \"M. Clerval\" (2) STILL separate\n   214→- ❌ \"Walton\" (6) and \"Captain Walton\" (1) STILL separate\n   215→- ❌ \"my mother\" (10) still separate from \"Madame Frankenstein\"\n   216→- ❌ Pronunciation false positives UNCHANGED (664 entries, ~50% common words)\n   217→- ✅ \"the creature\" (24) still correctly merged with aliases (maintained from Attempt 2)\n   218→- ✅ 25 chapters detected correctly\n   219→- ✅ Chapter summaries remain excellent\n   220→\n   221→**Analysis:** Diagnostic logging added but NO FIXES IMPLEMENTED. The logging changes only add observability - they don't change behavior. The analysis ran with the same broken logic as Attempt 3, so results are identical. Score: 6.25/10 (unchanged).\n   222→\n   223→**Critical Error:** Attempt 4 was supposed to ANALYZE THE LOGS and then IMPLEMENT A FIX based on findings. Instead, only logging was added and the system was re-run without any behavioral changes. This wasted an attempt.\n   224→\n   225→**Next Action:** Must analyze the diagnostic logs to identify root cause, THEN implement an actual fix to the merge logic.\n   226→\n   227→## Previous Text: gatsby\n   228→- **Result:** FAILED after 5 attempts (4.05/10)\n   229→- **Status:** Marked complete in manifest.json\n   230→\n   231→## Output Files (Attempt 4)\n   232→- HTML: output/frankenstein/report.html (generated Jan 18 06:10)\n   233→-